-- Source module: Solutions.R6Ifaces
/-!
# Round six: the stack interfaces of the top-level assembly (fixed statements)

This file fixes the names and statements of every stack interface that the round-six top-level
assembly `kappa_final6` (file `R6MFinal.lean`) takes as a hypothesis. Each one is a `Prop`
depending on the parameter record `P : Prm` (and, where it runs inside the machine's table, on
the Lemma 12 table `tab` of the bit network). The interfaces are

| name | piece | intended `Ncost6` row (margin) |
|---|---|---|
| `SetupNeed6` | §9.2 parameters, sources (sieve), register file | lower order (`O(V)` suffices) |
| `CrtNeed6` | `Φ` / `Φ⁻¹` with the E′ CRT reversal | `d` (`1-ε`) and `ℓ (d ln p)^τ` (`max(ε,1-ε)(1-τ)`) |
| `FineNeed6` | fine-bit exposure (Idea A) | feeds `d p^δ` (`1-ε-poly`) |
| `LineNeed6` | `A` lines (PR #5 chirped Gaussian), `B₀` lines (segmented inverse) | `d p^δ` (`1-ε-poly`) |
| `P14Need6` | the uniform Prop 14 `P14UH'` (file `R6IL3Iface2`; proved in `R6IL3Cfg6`) | `ℓ d^λ'` (`ε(1-λ')`) |
| `P18IL6` | Prop 18 from `P14UH'` | `ℓ d^λ'`, `d`, `ℓ + log₂ p` (`ε`), `p^δ` |

**Weakness.** Every cost bound is stated against the whole unit
`cU6 P n A = V · Ncost6 · (log lg n + 1)^A` (the assembly makes a bounded number of calls, so this
is all it needs); the docstrings name the row the construction is meant to meet. Every error
bound is `errW6 P n · 2^{-p} = 2^{⌊p/2⌋ - p}` (much larger than the frozen constants; the final
rounding has room for it since `γ = 2 d α² ≤ b'/4` and `p = 6 b'`). The interfaces are stated
only at the round-six parameters of `n` for `n ≥ n₁` (`n₁` chosen by the prover), for every
source list satisfying `SrcOK6`. The interfaces used inside the machine's table receive as
hypotheses everything the assembly has about the Lemma 12 table `tab` (`SwapNeedτ`, `RowUCP`,
`FineU6`, `P14UH`).

**Parameters** (all for `n` and `P`): digit bits `b' = b'P6`, `p = 6b'`, `L = LP6`, `T = 2^L`,
`d = dP6`, `ℓ = ℓP6`, `h = ℓ - 1`, `r = 2^ℓ`, `K = ℓ - 1`, the natural `α = αN6 = ⌊√(p/(48d))⌋`,
`γ = 2 d α²`, the number of half axes `d' = dℓ - L`; axis `j < d` has `t_j = 2^h` for `j < d'`
and `t_j = 2^{h+1}` for `j ≥ d'` (`tF6`), so `∏ t_j = T` and the last axis has length `r`.
Sources: `SrcOK6` (odd, pairwise coprime, `t_j - 2w_j < s_j ≤ t_j - w_j`, `w_j = ⌊t_j/(8d²)⌋`,
Jain's window with `η ≈ 1/(8d²) ≤ 1/(4 d L^ε)`), and `μ_j = (∏_{i<j} s_i)⁻¹ mod s_j` (`muR6`).
-/

