-- Source module: Solutions.R6IL3Cfg6
/-!
# Round six, item language (I3): the configuration of the complex network

**`cfg6_of`**: from a round-six complex network `J : Cx.Prop8IfaceH 207387136 T 576 Jain.cxR6`
in the gate class `GClassH J A`, the moment bound `histMoment cxR6 576 σ < 207387136` and the
depth guard `2 + 576 log(histRankSum cxR6) ≤ C1` (with `P.Ok`), the configuration
`c = cfg6 P J A` (`W = 207387136`, `T`, `m = 576`, `A`, `p = C1`, `net = netF J`) satisfies
`CfgOK c`, `c.p ≤ C1`, and the moment condition `hCc` of `p14UH'_of` at `τ = P.τ`,
`θ = max τ σ ≤ lampOf τ σ ≤ lamp` (some `Cc ≥ 0`).

**`p14Need6_of`** (the shape of the `P14Need6` switch): adding `IL.L12Canon tab l12 P.τ`,
`∃ Ew, IL3.P14UH' tab Ew P.lamp ∧ EwOK6 P Ew` (with `Ew = EwH c`).

## What `GClassH J A` requires (`Solutions/R6IL3Norm.lean`, `def GClassH`)

Every gate step `HStep.gate G ∈ J.net` (`G : Matrix (Fin W ⊕ Fin T) (Fin W ⊕ Fin T) ℂ`) is
either

* **a KFG atom list**: `∃ as : List NLogN.KFG.Atom`, `as.length ≤ A`, every atom `a` has
  `a.Ok (W + T)` and `a.h ≤ 1`, `NLogN.KFG.NoTS as`, and
  `G = (NLogN.KFG.gateMat (W + T) as).submatrix (roleEqv W T) (roleEqv W T)`.
  Here (`Solutions/KFGGate.lean`) an atom `⟨t, s, c, h⟩ : KFG.Atom` is `y_t += (c / 2^h) y_s`;
  `a.Ok W := a.t < W ∧ a.s < W ∧ a.t ≠ a.s ∧ Sm a.c` with `Sm c := |c.re| ≤ 1 ∧ |c.im| ≤ 1`
  (Gaussian integer, `Solutions/KFBGauss.lean`); `NoTS as := ∀ a b ∈ as, a.t ≠ b.s` (no target is
  a source); `gateMat W as p q = [p = q] + Σ_{a : t = p, s = q} c_a / 2^{h_a}`; the role numbering
  `roleEqv W T = finSumFinEquiv` (`Solutions/R6IL3Norm.lean`) puts data roles `0 … W-1` first
  and temporaries `W … W+T-1` after;
* **a `±1` role diagonal**: `∃ U : Finset (Fin W ⊕ Fin T)`,
  `G = Matrix.diagonal fun w => if w ∈ U then -1 else 1`.

The other step kinds (`rowAdd`, `phase`, `perm`, `child`) are unrestricted (children are
normalized by `Prop8IfaceH'.norm`).
-/

